# Auth requests: sign-up, login, and the 401 / 400 / 409 cases.
# Run `npm run seed` first (it creates the dummy accounts below).
#
# START HERE: send "loginOwner" first. Requests further down that need a token read it
# from that response. After reloading VS Code, send it again.
# Local: leave @baseUrl as is. Live: swap it for the deployed URL.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

###
# ---------- LOG IN (named, so later requests can reuse the token) ----------

### loginOwner -> 200 (token + staff, no password data)
# @name loginOwner
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "owner-password-123"
}

### loginStaffOne -> 200
# @name loginStaffOne
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff.one@example.com",
  "password": "staff-password-123"
}

### loginStaffTwo -> 200
# @name loginStaffTwo
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff.two@example.com",
  "password": "staff-password-123"
}

###
# ---------- SIGN UP ----------

### Sign up a new staff account -> 201 (the email changes on every send)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New Staff",
  "email": "new.staff.{{$timestamp}}@example.com",
  "password": "new-staff-password-1"
}

###
# ---------- USING A TOKEN ----------

### Protected route with a valid token -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

###
# ---------- FAILURE CASES ----------

### Sign up with a role in the body -> 400 (nobody can pick their own role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sneaky",
  "email": "sneaky@example.com",
  "password": "sneaky-password-1",
  "role": "owner"
}

### Password too short -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Short Password",
  "email": "short.password@example.com",
  "password": "short"
}

### Invalid email -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "long-enough-password"
}

### Email already registered -> 409 DUPLICATE_RECORD
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "staff.one@example.com",
  "password": "long-enough-password"
}

### Wrong password -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "not-the-password"
}

### Unknown email -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (same message as a wrong password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "whatever-password"
}

### Login with the password missing -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@example.com"
}

### Protected route with no token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders

### Protected route with a garbage token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer this-is-not-a-real-token
